# xynes-accounts-service .dockerignore — H-2 (group-H §`.dockerignore checklist`).
#
# Goal: keep the build context small AND prevent .env*, dev-only tooling,
# and test/docs payloads from bleeding into the prod image. The Dockerfile
# does explicit `COPY src ./src` etc., so the negative list here is
# defense in depth — anything we forget in this file but never `COPY` is
# already invisible to the prod stage.

# VCS metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Local-only env files (NEVER ship credentials in the image — env vars
# arrive via `-e` / compose / K8s at runtime)
.env
.env.*

# Dependency caches + build artefacts (Bun re-installs in-image)
node_modules
coverage
dist
.turbo
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Tests + test fixtures (excluded from prod image; CI runs `bun run test`
# outside the prod build)
test
tests
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.spec.ts
*.spec.tsx
**/__tests__/**
**/__mocks__/**

# Docs (kept in the repo, not the image)
README.md
DEVELOPER.md
docs

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.entire

# Dockerfile + .dockerignore themselves don't need to ship
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
